          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>No. In high price-to-rent ratio cities like Mumbai (30–45x) and large parts of Bangalore and Delhi, renting and systematically investing the difference in equity mutual funds can build more wealth over 15–20 years than buying. In Tier-2 cities where price-to-rent ratios are 12–20x, buying often makes clearer financial sense for those with a 7+ year horizon and a stable income.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="faq-item">
